{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumUniverses.QuantumUniverse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumUniverses.QuantumUniverse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Braided.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneBalancedRibbon","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Shapes.ZeroMorphisms","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Shapes.Kernels","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Preadditive.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Types.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.ContinuousMap.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Geometry.Manifold.IsManifold.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebra.Basic"],"declarations":43,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.differentialForms_isLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.differentialForms_isLimit","kind":"def","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L307-L307","doc":"The fork `differentialForms` is a limit: `Ω¹(A)` *is* the kernel of\n`μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.differentialForms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.differentialForms","kind":"def","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L304-L304","doc":"**`A` admits a universal first-order calculus.**  `Ω¹(A)` is a\nkernel of the multiplication `μ : A ⊗ A ⟶ A` in `C`: an object with a\nmorphism `ι : Ω¹(A) ⟶ A ⊗ A` such that `ι ≫ μ = 0`, universal among\nsuch.  This is the noncommutative universal calculus, not Mathlib's\n`KaehlerDifferential` (commutative only, and the quotient `I/I²` of\nthis kernel).  In `ModuleCat R` it is realised by\n`QOU.MathlibExt.UniversalDifferentials.Ω1`.  Carried as a fork plus\nits universal property rather than a `HasKernels C` instance: the\npaper needs this one kernel, not every kernel in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.dimQ_isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.dimQ_isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L294-L294","doc":"Every block's quantum dimension is a **unit**: each can be normalised\nagainst.  `IsUnit` for the same reason as `frobWeight_isUnit`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.dimQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.dimQ","kind":"def","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L291-L291","doc":"The quantum dimension `dim_q(λ)` of each block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobWeight_isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobWeight_isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L289-L289","doc":"Every block's Frobenius weight is a **unit**: none is invisible to the\ntrace.  `IsUnit`, not `≠ 0` — the paper says \"invertible in `R`\", and\nover a ring those differ (`2 ≠ 0` in `ℤ`, and `2` is not a unit).  The\ntwo coincide only over a field, which is why `≠ 0` survived while the\nbase ring was one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobWeight","kind":"def","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L283-L283","doc":"The Frobenius weight `∫_A p_λ` of each block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_complete","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L281-L281","doc":"**The blocks span.**  `Σ_λ p_λ = 𝟙_A`: every state resolves into the\nchannels, with nothing left over.  Together with orthogonality this is\nwhat \"Wedderburn decomposition\" means; without it the blocks could sit\ninside `A` without exhausting it.\n\nThis is the field the axiom's NAME promised and its TYPE did not\ndeliver.  It needs the finite sum that `Preadditive` supplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_orthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_orthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L273-L273","doc":"**Blocks do not mix.**  Distinct central idempotents are orthogonal, so a\nstate resolving into one channel has no component in another.  This is the\nhalf of semisimplicity that costs only a zero morphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_idem","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L269-L269","doc":"Each `p_λ` is idempotent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem","kind":"def","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L267-L267","doc":"The central idempotent `p_λ` of each block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.blocksFintype","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.blocksFintype","kind":"def","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L265-L265","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.blocks","kind":"def","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L264-L264","doc":"**Wedderburn semisimplicity** (axiom 4).  The substrate has *channels*:\n`A` decomposes into finitely many blocks that do not mix, and no block\nis degenerate.\n\nEncoded here: a `Fintype` of blocks, an idempotent endomorphism of `A`\nper block, their mutual orthogonality, their completeness, and\ninvertibility of each block's Frobenius weight and quantum dimension.\n\n**`blocks` indexes the NON-NEGLIGIBLE blocks, and vanishing elsewhere is\npermitted.**  `dimQ_isUnit` below is therefore a specification of what\n`blocks` ranges over, NOT a prohibition on the ambient category.  This\nmatters at a root of unity (and in char p), where some `dim_q(λ)` really\ndoes vanish: those λ are *negligible* — they form a tensor ideal, the\ncategorical trace kills anything factoring through them, and the standard\nconstruction quotients by that ideal (semisimplification) before reading\noff blocks.  Read as a prohibition, the field would exclude the\nroot-of-unity categories outright; read as an index specification, it\nsays the decomposition is that of the semisimplified quotient.\n\nThe corpus already relies on this shape elsewhere: `y_(1^3) ≡ 0` in\n`h3-markov-wenzl-weights` (the Temperley-Lieb quotient kills the 3-row\npartition), and `tr_M = Σ_λ y_λ χ^λ` sums over all λ with zero weights on\nsome.  That vanishing is a DIFFERENT mechanism from negligibility — a row\ncap at generic q, not a root-of-unity phenomenon — but it is the same\npattern, and it is why no sum over blocks needs re-indexing here.\n\nOrthogonality needs a zero morphism and completeness needs a finite\nsum; both come from the `Preadditive` instance field above.\n\n`frobWeight` and `dimQ` land in `R` via `unitEndEquiv`, which is\ncarried as a field rather than left to a docstring — see its comment\nfor why `R`-linearity alone does not supply it (bean `qou-w1g8`).\n\nGiven this axiom, the co-Casimir trace identity\n`tr_M(C_dimQ) = Σ_λ 1/dim_q(λ)` is a *consequence*, proved as\n`QOU.BraidKnot.frobenius_codim_universal` by linearity of the trace\nover the central idempotents.  It is deliberately NOT an axiom here:\nasserting it would assert something already proved, and would collide\nwith the unrelated `def:mass-identity` (the vortex integral). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.unitEndEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.unitEndEquiv","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L224-L224","doc":"**The ground ring is `End(𝟙_C)`.**  The block data below lands in `R`\nrather than in `End(𝟙_C)`, which presumes the two agree.  That is a\ngenuine extra assumption, NOT a consequence of `R`-linearity:\n`Linear R C` supplies only a ring map `R → End(𝟙_C)`, `r ↦ r • 𝟙`,\nand its being bijective needs `𝟙` simple.  Carried explicitly so the\nassumption is visible instead of hiding in a docstring.\n\nSurfaced on the paper side in `def:quantum-universe`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobenius_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobenius_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L214-L214","doc":"**Symmetric Frobenius** (axiom 3).  A closed loop has one amplitude:\nclosing a worldline on the left and closing it on the right compute the\nsame endomorphism of the unit.  Equivalently, the Frobenius form `∫_A`\nis symmetric and the Nakayama automorphism is trivial.\n\nThis is a genuine restriction, not a consequence of axiom 2: a Frobenius\nalgebra whose form is non-symmetric has `leftTrace ≠ rightTrace`, and\nthen \"the trace of a process\" — hence any mass read off a trace — would\ndepend on a drawing convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.fibreFunctor_unit_inhabited","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.fibreFunctor_unit_inhabited","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L204-L204","doc":"**Monoidality**: `ω(X ⊗ Y) ≅ ω(X) × ω(Y)` and `ω(𝟙) ≅ PUnit`.\nEncoded as: the image of the unit is inhabited. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.fibreFunctor_faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.fibreFunctor_faithful","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L196-L196","doc":"**Faithfulness**: `ω` reflects equality of morphisms.\nIf `ω.map f = ω.map g` then `f = g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.fibreFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.fibreFunctor","kind":"def","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L193-L193","doc":"The fibre functor `τ : C → Type*` (abstracting `Vect_R` / `R-Mod`).\nThe paper asks for it to be exact, faithful, `R`-linear and monoidal;\nNONE of those four is carried by this type, which is a bare functor to\n`Type`.  Recorded rather than silently implied — the gap is real and\nseparate from the `R`-linearity of `C` now carried above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobHopf","kind":"def","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L187-L187","doc":"The Frobenius–Hopf object `A` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.balancedInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.balancedInst","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L185-L185","doc":"**The balancing twist** `θ_X : X ⟶ X` (axiom 1, categorical half).\n\nThis is what makes the substrate parameter `q` *derivable rather than\ncarried*.  On the defining representation the twist axiom forces\n`θ_V = q^{1/2} · id_V` (`rem:sqrt-q-ribbon-structure`), so `q` is read\noff the structure; there is deliberately **no `q` field**, since a\ndistinguished element would smuggle in as data the thing the framework\nclaims to derive.\n\nThree further things it supplies, none of which the previous\n`[BraidedCategory]` alone gave:\n\n1. **Framing.**  Without a twist a braid closure is only a *framed* link\n   invariant — `tr_M(β)` depends on the writhe of the braid word rather\n   than on the knot.  Since masses are read off knots, that dependence\n   would be fatal.\n2. **Sphericality on all of `C`.**  Axiom 3 gives left-trace =\n   right-trace on `End(A)` only, but the Markov trace closes strands of\n   `V^{⊗n}`, not of `A`.  Ribbon = braided + spherical extends it to the\n   objects the knot theory actually uses.\n3. **A legible classical boundary.**  `BalancedCategory.ofSymmetric`\n   proves every symmetric category is balanced with `θ = 𝟙`, so the\n   classical case is `θ = 𝟙`, i.e. `q = 1` — a *describable member*, not\n   an excluded one.  This is why the fix is \"add the twist\", not \"forbid\n   symmetric\": `q → 1` must stay inside the category it is a limit of.\n\nUses the in-repo `BalancedCategory` (bean `rtrb`, sorry-free) since\nMathlib has no ribbon layer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.braidedInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.braidedInst","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L156-L156","doc":"**Temporal braiding.**  The exchange of two adjacent systems is a\nprocess with a direction: `c_{V,W} : V ⊗ W ≅ W ⊗ V`, not required to\nbe symmetric.  The hexagon identities are part of the class, and are\nwhat make an interaction independent of the order in which its\npairwise crossings are written. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.linInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.linInst","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L150-L150","doc":"**`C` is `R`-linear.**  Every hom-set is an `R`-module and composition\nis `R`-bilinear — verbatim `def:rigid-monoidal-category`, and what\n`def:quantum-universe` means by \"an `R`-linear braided monoidal\ncategory\".\n\nThis is `CategoryTheory.Linear`, which takes `Preadditive` as a\nprerequisite; the two are a stack, not alternatives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.preInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.preInst","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L142-L142","doc":"**Hom-sets are abelian groups.**  Carried because the paper's\n`R`-linearity (below) presupposes it, and because two axiom-4 fields\nneed it: the zero morphism for block orthogonality, and a finite sum\nfor block completeness.\n\nNote this REPLACES a bare `HasZeroMorphisms` field.  `Preadditive`\nsupplies zero morphisms already, so carrying both would put two\n`HasZeroMorphisms` instances on `C` and make `p_b ≫ p_b' = 0`\nambiguous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.monInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.monInst","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L132-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.catInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.catInst","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L131-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.C","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L130-L130","doc":"The monoidal category `C`. Represented as an opaque type with\n`Category` and `MonoidalCategory` instances. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.mk","kind":"ctor","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L127-L127","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse","kind":"structure","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L112-L307","doc":"**Quantum Universe** over a commutative ring `R`.\n\nA triple `(C, A, ω)` where `C` is a `k`-linear **braided** monoidal\ncategory, `A` is a Frobenius–Hopf object in `C`, and `ω` is a fibre\nfunctor.  The deformation parameter `q` is not part of the base\ndefinition; it enters via the substrate parameter\n(Definition 1.x, `SubstrateParameter`).\n\n**Rigidity is deliberately absent here.**  A quantum universe is\nbraided but need not have duals; duals are imposed one level up, on\n`QuantumObservableUniverse`, where they carry the antiparticles and\npermit a strand to close into a knot.  Do not add a `RigidCategory`\ninstance to this structure.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:quantum-universe}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:quantum-universe","label":"def:quantum-universe","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.rightTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.rightTrace","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L105-L108","doc":"**Right categorical trace** of `f : A → A`, closing the loop on the right:\n`𝟙 →[coev] A ⊗ A →[A ◁ f] A ⊗ A →[ev] 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.leftTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.leftTrace","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L100-L103","doc":"**Left categorical trace** of `f : A → A`, obtained by closing the loop on\nthe left: `𝟙 →[coev] A ⊗ A →[f ▷ A] A ⊗ A →[ev] 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.ev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.ev","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L96-L98","doc":"**Evaluation** `ev = μ ≫ ∫_A : A ⊗ A → 𝟙`.  Together with `coevaluation`\nand the two snake identities, this exhibits `A` as self-dual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobenius_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobenius_relation","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L88-L88","doc":"**Frobenius relation**: `μ ≫ Δ = (Δ ▷ A) ≫ α ≫ (A ◁ μ)`.\nComultiplication is a bimodule map — the defining axiom of a\nFrobenius object in a monoidal category. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.pairing_snake_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.pairing_snake_right","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L82-L82","doc":"**Snake identity (right).**  The composite\n`A →[λ_⁻¹] 𝟙 ⊗ A →[coev ▷ A] (A ⊗ A) ⊗ A →[α] A ⊗ (A ⊗ A)\n →[A ◁ ev] A ⊗ 𝟙 →[ρ_] A`\nequals `id_A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.pairing_snake_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.pairing_snake_left","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L75-L75","doc":"**Snake identity (left).**  The composite\n`A →[ρ⁻¹] A ⊗ 𝟙 →[A ◁ coev] A ⊗ (A ⊗ A) →[α⁻¹] (A ⊗ A) ⊗ A\n →[ev ▷ A] 𝟙 ⊗ A →[λ_] A`\nequals `id_A`, where `ev = μ ≫ λ`.  This is one half of the exact\nself-pairing making `A` self-dual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.coevaluation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.coevaluation","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Coevaluation morphism `η̃ : 𝟙 → A ⊗ A`, the dual datum to the\nevaluation `ev = μ ≫ λ : A ⊗ A → 𝟙`.  Together with `ev`, this\nexhibits `A` as self-dual in the monoidal category `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusForm","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Frobenius form `λ : A → 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L63-L63","doc":"Antipode morphism `S : A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.counit","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Counit morphism `ε : A → 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.comul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.comul","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Comultiplication morphism `Δ : A → A ⊗ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.unit","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Unit morphism `η : 𝟙 → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mul","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Multiplication morphism `μ : A ⊗ A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.obj","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L53-L53","doc":"The underlying object in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData","kind":"structure","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.lean#L42-L89","doc":"**Frobenius–Hopf data** in a monoidal category.\n\nAn object `A` equipped with a Hopf algebra structure `(μ, η, Δ, ε, S)` and\na Frobenius form `λ : A → 𝟙` such that the pairing `A ⊗ A → μ → A → λ → 𝟙`\nis non-degenerate and the Frobenius relation holds.\n\nLaTeX: used in `\\label{def:quantum-universe}`, item (ii).\nRef: [kock2004] ","signatureChunk":0}]}